INT. BRIGHTSTART FERTILITY CLINIC - WAITING ROOM - DAY

SUPER: "TUESDAY. 9:47 AM."

Gordon, 40s, rumpled and sweating through a pastel polo, grips a paper cup and a clipboard. Tess, 20s, behind the front desk, smiles a smile that has seen things.

INSERT - CLIPBOARD

Line 14: "Sample collected at home? Y / N". Gordon's pen hovers. He circles Y. Then N. Then Y.

BACK TO SCENE

TESS
Mr. Pruitt, Dr. Halloran will see you shortly.

GORDON
Great. Fantastic. Shortly. Love shortly.

His phone BUZZES. He answers, too loud.

GORDON (CONT'D)
Ros? I'm here, I'm in the, I'm at the place.

ROSALIND (V.O.)
(tinny, speakerphone)
Did you bring it. Gordon. Did you bring it.

GORDON
Define "it".

ROSALIND (V.O.)
The jar, Gordon. The jar in the cooler bag, in the car, in the August heat.

Gordon looks at the empty cup in his hand. Looks at the door.

POV - THROUGH THE WINDOW

The parking lot. His Subaru. Its trunk wide open. A Seagull the size of a toddler perches on the bumper.

BACK TO SCENE

A woman in sunglasses and a long coat sits two chairs down, reading a pamphlet upside down. She has been there since the top of the scene. She has not blinked.

GORDON
(to himself)
Okay. Okay okay okay.

Dr. Halloran, 50s, bow tie, enters from the hallway with a tablet. He and Gordon lock eyes. He raises a hand to wave. He sees the open trunk through the window. He lowers it.

ANGLE ON THE WOMAN

She stands. Slowly. She opens the coat. Inside, a cooler bag, sweating, strapped to her like a bomb vest.

THE WOMAN
Is this what you're looking for.

Gordon and Halloran both freeze. Tess drops her stapler.

GORDON
You STOLE my

THE WOMAN
I RESCUED your

DR. HALLORAN
Everybody stay calm, that is a biohazard and also a federal, I think, a federal something.

ROSALIND (V.O.)
What's happening. Why is everyone yelling. Gordon!

Gordon lunges for the bag. The woman spins away. Halloran grabs him, he grabs the coat, and all three of them crash into the pamphlet rack. Pamphlets rain down like confetti. Tess ducks under the desk.

INTERCUT - PARKING LOT / WAITING ROOM

The seagull hops into the trunk. It emerges with a sandwich. Nobody sees.

THE WOMAN
(pinned, furious)
Bev! My name is Bev! I'm Rosalind's sister, you absolute walnut, she sent me to make sure you'd show up!

Silence. Gordon, face down in pamphlets, slowly raises one finger.

GORDON
...Did she also send you to steal it?

BEV
No. That was freelance.

ROSALIND (V.O.)
Oh my god. Bev. I said WATCH him. Not ambush him.

Tess pops up from behind the desk, holding the cooler bag by one strap.

TESS
So, uh. Who's paying the co-pay.
